 The equation of the line can be written as $y = kx + b$. Substituting the points $(1, 7)$ and $(3, 11)$ into this equation, we get: \[
\begin{cases} 
7 = k \cdot 1 + b \\
11 = k \cdot 3 + b 
\end{cases}
\] Solving this system of equations, we get: \[
\begin{cases} 
k = 2 \\
b = 5 
\end{cases}
\] Therefore, the equation of the line is $y = 2x + 5$. Substituting $x = 0$ into this equation, we get $y = 5$. So, the line intersects the $y$-axis at the point $(0, 5)$. </think> <answer> $(0, 5)$ </answer>

