response:
 The probability that a single die shows a 1 is \(\frac{1}{6}\), and the probability that it does not show a 1 is \(\frac{5}{6}\). The probability that at most 4 of the 5 dice will show a 1 is the complement of the probability that all 5 dice will show a 1. \[
P(\text{all 5 dice show a 1}) = \left(\frac{1}{6}\right)^5 = \frac{1}{7776}
\] Therefore, \[
P(\text{at most 4 dice show a 1}) = 1 - P(\text{all 5 dice show a 1}) = 1 - \frac{1}{7776} = \frac{7775}{7776}
\] </think> <answer> \(\frac{7775}{7776}\) </answer>

